  A: not covered -- returns every field, so each match is fetched.
  B: not covered -- _id is returned by default and is not in the index.
  C: not covered -- name is not in the index.
  D: covered -- every returned field comes from the index keys.

=== Verification (variant D) ===
[OK] FETCH stage eliminated: winning plan is PROJECTION_COVERED > IXSCAN, totalDocsExamined = 0.
     Uncovered (A) examined 170 documents for the same 170 results.
     Covered speedup vs A: 1.3x (1.966 -> 1.512 ms per query).

  Rules for a covered query: filter, sort and projection use only fields in one
  index; exclude _id unless it is in that index; and none of the fields may be an
  array (a multikey index like idx_tags can never cover a query).

  First 5 results of the covered query: [{'category': 'Electronics', 'price': 100.03, 'rating': 2.2}, {'category': 'Electronics', 'price': 100.52, 'rating': 2.2}, {'category': 'Electronics', 'price': 100.72, 'rating': 3.1}, {'category': 'Electronics', 'price': 100.92, 'rating': 2.3}, {'category': 'Electronics', 'price': 101.24, 'rating': 2.7}]

